x(t)=\frac{c^2}{a'}\left(\sqrt{1+(a't/c)^2}-1\right).$$
This hyperbola has future null asymptote $x=ct-c^2/a'$. A right-moving signal emitted from $x_0$ at $t=0$ follows $x=ct+x_0$; if $x_0<-c^2/a'$, it lies beyond that <acceleration> horizon and never intersects the worldline.

