$$E_{n_xn_yn_z}=\frac{\hbar^2\pi^2}{2m}\left(\frac{n_x^2}{a^2}+\frac{n_y^2}{b^2}+\frac{n_z^2}{c^2}\right),\qquad n_x,n_y,n_z\ge1.$$
For $a<b<c$, the ground state $(1,1,1)$ is nondegenerate. The cheapest excitation changes the quantum number in the longest direction, so the first excited state $(1,1,2)$ is also nondegenerate.

If $a<b=c$, the ground state remains nondegenerate, but $(1,2,1)$ and $(1,1,2)$ have equal first-excited energy, giving degeneracy two.

