$$\alpha_1=\frac{u+v}{3},\qquad
\alpha_2=\frac{\omega^2u+\omega v}{3},\qquad
\alpha_3=\frac{\omega u+\omega^2v}{3}.$$
These expressions use only square and cube roots. A general cubic is first translated to remove its quadratic term, proving the existence of a formula by radicals.

