For $X^3-21X-22$,
$$\Delta=23976=2^3\,3^4\,37$$
is not a square, so the Galois <group> is $S_3$.

For $X^3-21X-28$,
$$\Delta=15876=126^2,$$
so the Galois <group> is $A_3\cong C_3$.

Finally,
$$X^3-21X-34=(X+2)(X^2-2X-17),$$
whose remaining roots are $1\pm3\sqrt2$. Its splitting field is $\mathbb Q(\sqrt2)$ and its Galois <group> is $C_2$.

